Q: Using Package Dio in Flutter - sending multiple images(multipart) under one key A: <p>if the back accepts a list of Multipart file in a field called <code>images</code>, you could try the following:</p>
<pre><code>  Future&lt;FormData&gt; toFormData()async{
    return FormData.fromMap({
      'name' : name,

      for(int i = 0 ; i &lt; images.length ; i++)
        'images[$i]' : await MultipartFile.fromFile(
          images[i], filename: images[i].path.split('/').last,),

    });
  }
</code></pre>
<p>this way the back see and accept all images as <strong>list</strong>, but the technique you are using in the question will lead to a duplicated entries.</p>
<p>You could encapsulate the above method within your model and call it when giving the model to <code>dio</code>.</p>

Q: VSCode: Select entire function definition? A: <p>If using the plugin <code>vim-indent-object</code>, you can do the steps @userrandrand provided in their answer.</p>
<p>And to extend on that, if you want to select the function you are in, <strong>wherever you are</strong>, you can add a map for <code>vaf</code> that do a reverse search for the function keyword, like <code>def</code> for Python, go down a line and do a <code>vai</code>.</p>
<p>In VSCode, this mapping could be like this:</p>
<pre class="lang-json prettyprint-override"><code>    &quot;vim.normalModeKeyBindingsNonRecursive&quot;: [
        {
            // Select Python function
            &quot;before&quot;: [&quot;v&quot;, &quot;a&quot;, &quot;f&quot;],
            &quot;after&quot;: [&quot;?&quot;, &quot;d&quot;, &quot;e&quot;, &quot;f&quot;, &quot; &quot;, &quot;&lt;enter&gt;&quot;, &quot;j&quot;, &quot;v&quot;, &quot;a&quot;, &quot;i&quot;]
        },
    ],
</code></pre>
